       Software in academic papers, theses, dissertations, technical reports,
       or conference presentations, provided you accurately attribute the work
       to the Author and clearly identify MedDelta-RAG as the source.

  3.2  You may REPRODUCE SMALL EXCERPTS of the source code (no more than 20
       consecutive lines) in academic publications solely for the purpose of
       illustrating the described methodology, provided such use is accompanied
       by a full citation.

  3.3  You may RUN the Software on your local machine for the purpose of
       reproducing the experimental results described in the associated
       research paper, provided you do not distribute your results in a manner
       that misrepresents them as independent original research.

